{"name":"Erythrosine","hex":"#fc7ab0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"erythrosine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["tetraiodo-fluorescein, a cherry-pink fluorone used as a food colouring, in printing inks, and as a biological stain, a dental plaque disclosing agent and a radiopaque medium."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/erythrosine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Erythrosine","blocks":[{"text":"Erythrosine, also known as E127 and Red No. 3, is an organoiodine compound, specifically a derivative of fluorone. It is a red-pink dye used for food coloring, cosmetics, hair coloring, pet products, and diverse industrial colorings. It is the disodium salt of 2,4,5,7-tetraiodofluorescein."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Erythrosine.svg/330px-Erythrosine.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erythrosine"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"erythrosine":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ad/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-erythrosine.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/ad/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-erythrosine.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-erythrosine.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/ad/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-erythrosine.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-erythrosine.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Burano Hausfassade Wäsche-20090315-RM-113043","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg/500px-Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-RM-113043.jpg","ratio":0.7864328830123599,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Burano_Hausfassade_W%C3%A4sche-20090315-R